      "gridPos": {
        "h": 5,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 46
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**Source.** Kyverno controller metrics (`kyverno_*`) from the four controller metrics services, plus container metrics from cAdvisor and kube-state-metrics. Names and labels checked against Kyverno v1.19.1.\n\n- Policy results count rule evaluations, not distinct resources. A background scan re-counts the same failing resource every cycle.\n- By default Kyverno does not export `policy_namespace` and `resource_namespace` labels, so results are per policy and kind, not per namespace.\n- Current violations per resource are in Policy Reporter (https://kyverno.jokelab.dev); this dashboard shows evaluation activity and controller health.\n- Counters appear after their first event, so empty panels on a quiet cluster are normal."
      }
